        ["abaqus/2025"] = {
          Version = "2025",
          canonical = "2025",
          fn = "/usr/local/pace-apps/manual/modules/lmod/linux-rhel9-x86_64/Core/abaqus/2025.lua",
          help = [[        Abaqus 2025 — SIMULIA Established Products
        ============================================================

        Abaqus is a finite element analysis (FEA) suite for structural,
        thermal, and multiphysics simulations. This installation includes
        Abaqus/Standard, Abaqus/Explicit, Abaqus CAE, Tosca, fe-safe,
        and Isight. Both CPU and GPU execution are supported out of the
        box — no separate GPU-enabled build is needed. GPU acceleration
        is available for Abaqus/Standard's iterative solver and
        Abaqus/Explicit at runtime by simply passing gpus=N to the
        abaqus command.

        To load:
            module load abaqus/2025
        To unload:
            module unload abaqus/2025
        ── Module Behavior ──────────────────────────────────────────
        When loading this module, any loaded MPI modules (mvapich2 or
        openmpi) will be automatically unloaded. This is because Abaqus
        ships with its own internal MPI implementation and conflicts with
        system MPI libraries can cause jobs to fail or hang.

        ── License ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
        Abaqus uses a FlexNet license server managed by COE IT (not PACE):
            2002@abaquslic.ecs.gatech.edu
        For license issues contact: coe-software@coe.gatech.edu

        ── GPU Support ──────────────────────────────────────────────
        Abaqus supports GPU acceleration for:
          - Abaqus/Standard iterative solver
          - Abaqus/Explicit
        To use GPU, request a GPU node via SLURM and pass gpus=N to Abaqus:
            abaqus job=myjob input=myjob.inp gpus=1 mp_mode=threads cpus=4

        ── Running Jobs ─────────────────────────────────────────────
        Basic CPU job:
            abaqus job=myjob input=myjob.inp cpus=4 interactive

        GPU job (on a GPU node):
            abaqus job=myjob input=myjob.inp gpus=1 mp_mode=threads cpus=4 interactive

        ── Examples ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
        Ready-to-run CPU and GPU examples are provided. To try them:

            # CPU example
            cp -r $ABAQUS_ROOT/examples/cpu_test /tmp/abaqus_cpu_test
            cd /tmp/abaqus_cpu_test
            abaqus job=test_cpu input=test_cpu.inp interactive

            # GPU example (run on a GPU node)
            cp -r $ABAQUS_ROOT/examples/gpu_test /tmp/abaqus_gpu_test
            cd /tmp/abaqus_gpu_test
            abaqus job=test_gpu input=test_gpu.inp gpus=1 mp_mode=threads cpus=4 interactive

        ── More Info ────────────────────────────────────────────────
        PACE support: pace-support@oit.gatech.edu
        SIMULIA docs: https://www.3ds.com/products/simulia/abaqus

