          help = [[Firedrake 2024 - Finite Element PDE Solver
===========================================

Firedrake is an automated system for solving partial differential equations
using the finite element method. This is a containerized installation.

*** IMPORTANT: This module only works on compute nodes (not login nodes) ***
    Get a compute node: salloc --account=<account> -N 1 --ntasks=1 -t 1:00:00


QUICK START
-----------
*** Get a compute node first: salloc --account=<account> -N 1 --ntasks=1 -t 1:00:00 ***

Example scripts available in $FIREDRAKE_EXAMPLES

Interactive exploration:
  module load firedrake/2024
  apptainer shell --cleanenv $FIREDRAKE_SIF
  python3
  >>> from firedrake import *

Serial job:
  module load firedrake/2024
  cp $FIREDRAKE_EXAMPLES/serial_poisson.py .
  apptainer exec --cleanenv $FIREDRAKE_SIF python3 serial_poisson.py


INTERACTIVE USAGE
-----------------
*** Requires compute node ***

For interactive Python session:
  module load firedrake/2024
  apptainer shell --cleanenv $FIREDRAKE_SIF
  python3

  # Inside Python:
  >>> from firedrake import *
  >>> mesh = UnitSquareMesh(10, 10)
  >>> print(f"Mesh has {mesh.num_vertices()} vertices")

Or run the interactive demo:
  cp $FIREDRAKE_EXAMPLES/interactive_demo.py .
  apptainer exec --cleanenv $FIREDRAKE_SIF python3 interactive_demo.py


SERIAL USAGE (Single Core)
---------------------------
*** Requires compute node ***

Run your own script:
  module load firedrake/2024
  apptainer exec --cleanenv $FIREDRAKE_SIF python3 my_script.py

Or try the example:
  module load firedrake/2024
  cp $FIREDRAKE_EXAMPLES/serial_poisson.py .
  apptainer exec --cleanenv $FIREDRAKE_SIF python3 serial_poisson.py


PARALLEL USAGE (Multiple Cores/Nodes)
--------------------------------------
*** Requires compute node with SLURM allocation ***

Parallel jobs require a wrapper script and one-time setup.

Step 1: First-time setup (copy example scripts):
  module load firedrake/2024
  cp $FIREDRAKE_EXAMPLES/firedrake_srun.sh .
  cp $FIREDRAKE_EXAMPLES/precompile.py .
  chmod +x firedrake_srun.sh

Step 2: Pre-compile JIT cache (run once per user):
  apptainer exec --cleanenv $FIREDRAKE_SIF python3 precompile.py

Step 3: Load additional modules and run:
  module load gcc/12 mvapich2 firedrake/2024
  ./firedrake_srun.sh my_parallel_script.py

Or test with provided example:
  cp $FIREDRAKE_EXAMPLES/test_firedrake_parallel.py .
  ./firedrake_srun.sh test_firedrake_parallel.py

See $FIREDRAKE_EXAMPLES/README.md for details.


BATCH JOB EXAMPLE
-----------------
*** Copy firedrake_srun.sh and precompile.py from $FIREDRAKE_EXAMPLES first ***

Create submit.sbatch:

  #!/bin/bash
  #SBATCH -J firedrake_job
  #SBATCH -N 2
  #SBATCH --ntasks-per-node=8
  #SBATCH -t 1:00:00
  #SBATCH -q inferno
  
  # Load environment
  module load gcc/12 mvapich2 firedrake/2024
  
  # Pre-compile JIT cache in serial (prevents race conditions)
  apptainer exec --cleanenv $FIREDRAKE_SIF python3 precompile.py
  
  # Run parallel job
  chmod +x firedrake_srun.sh
  ./firedrake_srun.sh my_script.py

Before first submission:
  cp $FIREDRAKE_EXAMPLES/firedrake_srun.sh .
  cp $FIREDRAKE_EXAMPLES/precompile.py .

Submit: sbatch submit.sbatch


ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
---------------------
$FIREDRAKE_SIF       - Path to container file
$FIREDRAKE_EXAMPLES  - Example scripts directory
$FIREDRAKE_VERSION   - Version (2024)


EXAMPLE SCRIPTS AVAILABLE
--------------------------
$FIREDRAKE_EXAMPLES/serial_poisson.py          - Simple serial Poisson solver
$FIREDRAKE_EXAMPLES/interactive_demo.py        - Interactive demonstration
$FIREDRAKE_EXAMPLES/test_firedrake_parallel.py - Parallel test script
$FIREDRAKE_EXAMPLES/firedrake_srun.sh          - Parallel wrapper script
$FIREDRAKE_EXAMPLES/precompile.py              - JIT cache pre-compiler
$FIREDRAKE_EXAMPLES/README.md                  - Detailed usage guide


TROUBLESHOOTING
---------------
- Module won't load? Must be on compute node (not login node)
- Parallel job fails? Must load gcc/12 and mvapich2 modules
- Python package conflicts? Use: apptainer exec --no-home $FIREDRAKE_SIF ...

Documentation: https://www.firedrakeproject.org/
