          help = [[This module sets up Gurobi Optimizer 13.0.1 with GPU support (CUDA 12).
 
================================================================================
QUICK START
================================================================================
 
Command-line solver (no Python):
    module load gurobi/13.0.1
    gurobi_cl model.lp
 
Test examples (after setting up Python - see PYTHON USAGE below):
    python3 $GUROBI_HOME/examples/gpu_test_simple.py
    python3 $GUROBI_HOME/examples/gpu_test_full.py
 
================================================================================
PYTHON USAGE
================================================================================
 
This module works with ANY Python version (3.10, 3.11, 3.12, 3.13, 3.14+).
Create your own environment and install gurobipy + any packages you need.
 
Example setup:
    module load python/3.14  # Or any version you prefer
    python3 -m venv ~/myenv
    source ~/myenv/bin/activate
    pip install gurobipy numpy scipy pandas  # Install what you need
    module load gurobi/13.0.1
    unset PYTHONPATH  # Avoid conflicts (module sets this for legacy Python 3.11)
    
    # Run your script or test examples
    python3 your_script.py
    python3 $GUROBI_HOME/examples/gpu_test_simple.py
 
For conda users: 
    Install gurobipy via pip in your conda environment (not available in conda-forge).
 
Why unset PYTHONPATH? 
    This module includes legacy Python 3.11 bindings (gurobipy only, no other packages).
    If using a different Python version or your own environment, unset PYTHONPATH
    to avoid import conflicts.
 
================================================================================
GPU ACCELERATION (Beta Feature)
================================================================================
 
GPU acceleration requires Python with gurobipy installed.
Set up your Python environment first (see PYTHON USAGE above).
 
To use GPU acceleration with the PDHG algorithm:
 
1. Set up Python environment and load modules:
    # After creating your environment (venv or conda) with gurobipy installed
    module load gurobi/13.0.1 cuda/12.6.1
    unset PYTHONPATH  # If using custom environment
 
2. Request GPU node in SLURM script:
    #SBATCH --gres=gpu:1
    #SBATCH -q inferno
 
3. Enable GPU in your Python code:
    import gurobipy as gp
    from gurobipy import GRB
    
    model = gp.Model("example")
    # ... add variables, constraints, objective ...
    
    # Enable PDHG with GPU
    model.setParam('Method', 6)      # PDHG algorithm
    model.setParam('PDHGGPU', 1)     # Enable GPU acceleration
    
    model.optimize()
 
Test GPU functionality:
    python3 $GUROBI_HOME/examples/gpu_test_simple.py
    python3 $GUROBI_HOME/examples/gpu_test_full.py
 
Note: GPU support is a beta feature. The solver will fall back to CPU if:
  - No GPU is available
  - CUDA libraries are not loaded
  - The problem is not suitable for GPU acceleration
 
================================================================================
TECHNICAL DETAILS
================================================================================
 
Version:        13.0.1
CUDA Support:   CUDA 12.9
Python:         Works with any version (3.10+) - install gurobipy in your environment
                (Legacy Python 3.11 bindings included but not recommended)
License:        Academic (ID: 2441885)
Expiration:     2026-11-20
Architecture:   x86_64 (works on CPU and GPU nodes)
 
This version works on all node types:
  - CPU nodes: Full functionality, no GPU needed
  - GPU nodes: Optional GPU acceleration when CUDA is loaded
 
For issues or questions:
    pace-support@oit.gatech.edu
]],
