          help = [[This module allows you to run Ollama 0.12.11 from an Apptainer image.  

Before running Ollama, make sure you create a symlink named `~/.ollama` that
points to a directory on your project, data, or scratch space.  This can be
accomplished by:

    * On Phoenix:  
  
          mkdir ~/project/.ollama
          ln -s ~/project/.ollama ~/.ollama
  
    * On Hive:  
  
          mkdir ~/data/.ollama
          ln -s ~/data/.ollama ~/.ollama
  
    * On ICE:
  
          mkdir ~/scratch/.ollama
          ln -s ~/scratch/.ollama ~/.ollama

Next, start the Ollama backend server.  This can be done in a few ways:

    * Option 1: Run the server as a background process:
  
          ollama serve &
  
      If you'd like to keep a logfile for the server, you can instead do:
  
          ollama serve &> ollama.log &
  
    * Option 2: Run the server as a containerized service:
  
        apptainer instance run --nv $OLLAMA_SIF ollama-server

After the Ollama server is running, you can interact with it using `ollama run`, 
REST APIs, and Python APIs.

To make sure Ollama is running, run `curl http://127.0.0.1:11434` (11434 is
Ollama's default port). The curl command should return `Ollama is running`.

To quickly run or test a model, run `ollama run gemma3:270m`. This will
download the model (if not already in your cache).
]],
