          help = [[This module allows you to run ollama 0.5.1 from an Apptainer image.

Before running ollama, make sure you create a symlink named `~/.ollama` that
points to a directory on your project, data, or scratch space.  This can be
accomplished by:

* On Phoenix:  

    mkdir ~/project/.ollama
    ln -s ~/project/.ollama ~/.ollama

* On Hive:  

    mkdir ~/data/.ollama
    ln -s ~/data/.ollama ~/.ollama

* On ICE:

    mkdir ~/scratch/.ollama
    ln -s ~/scratch/.ollama ~/.ollama

To run an interactive chat with a model from ollama.com, use `ollama run`

   ollama run smollm

You can also run from a model imported via a .gguf file.  See the ollama docs
for more info:

  https://github.com/ollama/ollama?tab=readme-ov-file#import-from-gguf

You can also start an ollama server as a backend service, which allows you to
connect to it via a frontend service like curl, Python, or many others.  First,
use Apptainer to start an instance of the ollama server with NVIDIA GPU
support:

    apptainer instance run --nv "$OLLAMA_SIF" ollama-server

After that, you can connect to a server via the frontend of your choice.  When
you are finished, you can stop the ollama server with:

    apptainer instance stop ollama-server
]],
