container: https://www.bioconductor.org/help/docker/

Basic Usage:

  After loading this module (`module load r/4.2.1-bio`), 
  the `R` and `Rscript` commands are available.  These will run 
  R in the container, and no additional setup is required.  They
  will accept the same command line options as the usual `R` and 
  `Rscript` commands.  These commands will work in both interactive 
  sessions and batch scripts.

Advanced Usage:

  For more elaborate use cases, you can directly invoke Apptainer.  
  After loading this module, the `R_SIF` environment variable will have 
  the path of the Apptainer image file (.sif).  Then use 
  `apptainer shell` or `apptainer exec` to execute commands within 
  the container.  

  For example, if you want to run code with GPU support, you would use
  something like `apptainer exec --nv $R_SIF Rscript my_script.R`.  
  For more info, see the Apptainer docs: 
  https://apptainer.org/user-docs/master/gpu.html
]],
