          help = [[This module provides uv v0.7.12

uv is a Python package manager with increased performance compared to pip, conda, and mamba.  It provides advanced workflows for installing, packaging, and distributing Python projects.  Below, we show how to use it as a drop-in replacement for venv and pip (https://docs.astral.sh/uv/pip/). 

1. Create a new virtual environment.  The path can be any directory for which you have write access.  We recommend using a path in your ~/project space (on Phoenix) or ~/scratch space (on ICE).

   uv venv ~/project/my-torch-env

2. Activate the environment.  This needs to be done every time you want to use the environment.

   source ~/project/my-torch-env/bin/activate

3. Install your packages.  In this example, we install pytorch using the same package names and sources that would be used with a normal `pip install`
 
    uv pip install torch torchvision torchaudio --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu128
]],
