          help = [[  This module loads vasp/6.4.2 built with nvhpc 24.5 with HDF5 support.
  vasp is a modeling software used for molecular analysis, mainly used by researchers.
  Only licensed users can use this software.
  For more information on licenses, testing, and running vasp, see here: https://gatech.service-now.com/home?id=kb_article_view&sysparm_article=KB0041636

  To run vasp/6.4.2, follow these steps:
        1) Load modules:
                $ module purge
                $ module load nvhpc/24.5
                $ module load hpcx/2.19-cuda
                $ module load vasp/6.4.2-hdf5
        2) Run vasp using the following commands:
                $ vasp_std
                $ vasp_gam
                $ vasp_ncl

  To run a quick test, please follow these steps:
        1) Allocate a GPU node:
                $ salloc -A<charge account> -qembers -N2 -n4 --gres=gpu:V100:2
        2) Once a GPU node has been allocated, run the following commands to copy the vasp testsuite:
                $ module purge
                $ module load nvhpc/24.5
                $ module load hpcx/2.19-cuda
                $ module load vasp/6.4.2-hdf5
                $ cd ~/scratch
                $ cp -r "${VASP_ROOT}"/simpletest .
                $ cd simpletest 
                $ srun --mpi=pmix vasp_std &> VASP_job.out.$SLURM_JOB_ID (be aware that test might run longer, you can stop it any time), or modify submit.batch and run sbatch submit.batch 
        3) Test output 
                $ cat VASP_job.out.$SLURM_JOB_ID 

]],
