Compiling a C Program:  After loading the module, you can
compile and link a program to NetCDF with a compile line
like this (Note the -I, -L, and -l flags):

  mpicc -o YOUR_PROGRAM YOUR_SOURCE.c -I$NETCDF_C_ROOT/include -L$NETCDF_C_ROOT/lib -lnetcdf

Example: Two test programs (simple_xy_rd and simple_xy_wr for reading/writing)
can be compiled and run in a job:

  cp -r $NETCDF_C_ROOT/pace-examples .
  cd pace-examples
  make
  srun ./simple_xy_rd
  srun ./simple_xy_wr
]],
