          help = [[  This module loads vasp 6.4.2 built with openmpi-4.1.5 and intel-2021.9.0.
  This includes the vaspsol++ modifications (https://github.com/VASPsol/VASPsol/).
  vasp is a modeling software used for molecular analysis, mainly used by researchers.
  Only licensed users can use this software.
  For more information on licenses, testing, and running vasp, see here: https://gatech.service-now.com/home?id=kb_article_view&sysparm_article=KB0041636

  To run vasp 6.4.2-vaspsolpp, follow these steps:
        1) Load modules:
                $ module purge
                $ module load intel/2021.9.0
  		$ module load openmpi/4.1.5
                $ module load vasp/6.4.2-vaspsolpp 
        2) Run vasp using the following commands:
                $ vasp_std
                $ vasp_gam
                $ vasp_ncl

  To run a test from the included test suite, please follow these steps:
        1) Allocate a CPU node:
                $ salloc -A<charge account> -qembers -N2 -n4
        2) Once a node has been allocated, run the following commands to copy the vasp testsuite:
                $ mkdir ~/scratch/vasp-test-"${SLURM_JOB_ID}"
                $ cd ~/scratch/vasp-test-"${SLURM_JOB_ID}"
                $ module purge
                $ module load intel/2021.9.0
                $ module load openmpi/4.1.5
                $ module load vasp/6.4.2-vaspsolpp 
                $ cp -r "${VASP_ROOT}/testsuite" .
                $ cd testsuite
                $ export VASP_TESTSUITE_EXE_GAM="srun vasp_gam"
                $ export VASP_TESTSUITE_TESTS="andersen_nve_constrain_fixed"
                $ ./runtest
                For more information on testing, see https://www.vasp.at/wiki/index.php/Validation_tests
        3) Test output
                ...
                ==================================================================
                SUCCESS: ALL SELECTED TESTS PASSED
                ==================================================================
]],
