          help = [[FreeFEM++ 4.15 — Finite Element PDE Solver
Built with UMFPACK (direct sparse solver via SuiteSparse), PETSc, MPI, and OpenMPI.

Usage (serial):
  module load gcc/12.3.0 openmpi/4.1.8 freefem/4.15-ompi
  FreeFem++ -v 0 -nw your_script.edp

Usage (MPI parallel via sbatch):
  module load gcc/12.3.0 openmpi/4.1.8 freefem/4.15-ompi
  mpirun -np $SLURM_NTASKS FreeFem++-mpi -v 0 -nw your_script.edp

  Example sbatch header:
  #SBATCH --ntasks=8
  #SBATCH --nodes=1

Usage (GPU-accelerated via PETSc+CUDA — requires gpu node):
  module load gcc/12.3.0 openmpi/4.1.8 freefem/4.15-ompi-cuda
  # In your sbatch script: #SBATCH --gpus=1
  # Use PETSc GPU solvers in your FreeFEM script for GPU acceleration
  # See: https://doc.freefem.org/documentation/petsc.html

Example (lid-driven cavity with UMFPACK):
  mkdir -p ~/scratch/freefem-test && cd ~/scratch/freefem-test
  cp $FREEFEM_EXAMPLES/pace-hpc/lid-driven-cavity-umfpack.edp .
  FreeFem++ -v 1 -nw lid-driven-cavity-umfpack.edp

UMFPACK is the default sparse solver. Use solver=UMFPACK in your problem definitions.

Documentation: https://doc.freefem.org
